          "effect": "This is a short noun stack in the list of staging tests. The reader can work it out from the earlier sentence that a request at exactly lease_until is rejected. Saying it outright, for example '현재 시간이 정확히 lease_until인 경우', would read more smoothly.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ],
      "verdict": "pass",
      "reason": "The draft's material claims match the source. Claiming increments epoch, sets owner and lease_until from database time, and returns the epoch. Completion and renewal both require owner and epoch to match and database now < lease_until, so a request at exactly lease_until fails. Expiry does not stop the old process. Fencing blocks stale database writes but not duplicate computation. A rejected completion writes no result and sends no event. The outbox row is written in the same transaction, delivery may be duplicated, and consumers deduplicate by event_id. The design is implemented in staging only, five cases were tested, and there is no production record. The omitted items are the queue payload, the historical prototype, the unimplemented cancellation proposal, and the unfenced external payment call. The service has no payment integration, so none of these omissions removes a condition the reader needs. The draft explains each central term by what it does: owner, lease_until, epoch, fencing, outbox and the dispatcher. It keeps the code identifiers. A reader with basic software knowledge can follow why late completions are rejected."
    },
